Heavy Period Care Checklist: What to Keep Ready Before Your Period Starts

When your period is heavy, being prepared can save you from last-minute stress. Instead of waiting for your period to arrive, you can create a simple heavy-period care routine.

1. Keep Your Sanitary Pads Ready

Do not wait until your period starts to purchase your menstrual products.

Keep enough pads at home, especially if you know that your first few days are usually heavy.

TIME Ultra Velvet sanitary pads can be part of your menstrual-care essentials.

2. Carry Extra Pads

Keep several pads in your everyday handbag, backpack, or work drawer.

3. Prepare Spare Underwear

A spare pair can be useful if unexpected leakage occurs.

4. Keep Disposal Bags

Use suitable bags to wrap used sanitary pads before disposal.

5. Track Your Cycle

A period tracker can help you estimate when your period may begin and identify your heavier days.

6. Choose the Right Protection

Your sanitary pad should match your flow. Consider absorbency, length, coverage, comfort, and fit.

7. Plan for Night-Time

If your flow is heavy at night, prepare suitable overnight protection before going to bed.

8. Prepare for Travel

If you have travel plans around your expected period, pack more menstrual products than you think you will need.

9. Prioritise Comfort

Wear comfortable clothing and breathable underwear, and change your pad regularly.

10. Know When to Seek Medical Advice

If your menstrual bleeding becomes unusually heavy, lasts much longer than usual, or repeatedly affects your everyday life, consult a healthcare professional.

Your Heavy-Period Essentials

